# A UNC path (starting with `\`) gets the path help.
mode: syntax
---- query
'\\server\share\x.csv' | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..32
  PIPELINE@0..31
    LITERAL@0..22
      STRING@0..22 "'\\\\server\\share\\x.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
    PIPE@23..24 "|"
    WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
    TAKE_OP@25..31
      IDENT@25..29 "take"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      LITERAL@30..31
        LONG@30..31 "1"
  WHITESPACE@31..32 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\s`
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | '\\server\share\x.csv' | take 1
  |          ^^    -- `\x` is not valid either
  |          |
  |          not a valid escape
  |
  = help: if this is a Windows path, use a verbatim string `@'\\server\share\x.csv'` or forward slashes `'//server/share/x.csv'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`
